    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Facing First gen Gu Yue, the Kinship Bloodworm points toward him. Lord Sky Crane says he refined it from the heart blood of First gen Gu Yue’s two sons: they were only five to six years old, so he turned them into living sources and took blood every month for tens of years before the refine finished; both sons died soon after. He adds that even as a rank five Gu its range is limited, and for a long time he could not find the target in a world that large.",
        "chapters": [
          192
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "refine-and-target",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_first_gen_gu_yue"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "After breaking free of the ice, Lord Sky Crane finds Fang Zheng and realizes the twin resemblance. With a close relative on him, he could refine the Kinship Blood worm. He treats saving Fang Zheng as his only remaining hope on the assignment.",
        "chapters": [
          199
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
